<title>CHINA: Triplenic year net profit rises sharply.</title>
<headline>Triplenic year net profit rises sharply.</headline>
<dateline>HONG KONG 1997-07-04</dateline>
<text>
<p>Year ended March 31</p>
<p>(in million HK$ unless stated)</p>
<p>    Shr (H.K. cents)	   34.6	  vs 3.1 (adjusted)</p>
<p>    Dividend (H.K. cents)    6.0	   vs nil</p>
<p>    Exceptional items	  106.78 gain vs 0.62 gain</p>
<p>    Net			    128.01	vs 11.47</p>
<p>    Turnover		     380.35	vs 17.02</p>
<p>    Company name		 Triplenic Holdings Ltd</p>
<p>    Books close		  August 25-29</p>
<p>    Dividend payable	   November 7</p>
<p>NOTE - Triplenic, formerly Kai Ming Investment Co Ltd, is a property investment and development company.</p>
<p>The company proposed a bonus issue of one new share for every one existing share by capitalisation of retained profits.</p>
<p>Net is after an exceptional gain on disposal of investment properties.</p>
<p>Comparative share earnings has been adjusted for the subdivision of one ordinary share at HK$1 each to 8 ordinary shares at HK$0.125 each on July 31, 1996.</p>
<p>Total dividend for year is six H.K. cents vs one cent (adjusted).</p>
<p>-- Hong Kong Newsroom (852) 2843 6368</p>
</text>
